    "body": "> Side note, which @richard-townsend-arm can correct if wrong, the current Chromium code would wait to execute async scripts if a network boundary happened to come right after a single synchronous script. Which isn't great, of course.\r\n\r\nOK. I think it *is* good for predictable behavior (compared to sometimes blocking `async` scripts). I believe the spec tries its best to avoid different behavior depending on where network boundaries fall.",
